         <pdfx:SourceModified>D:20120124124722</pdfx:SourceModified>
         <pdfx:Company>SortilÃ¨ge ComTek B.V.</pdfx:Company>
         <pdfx:Manager>T</pdfx:Manager>
         <pdfx:Comments>txtTitle=CORA&#xD;txtSponsor=&#xD;txtDocNo1=SR&#xD;cboClass=1&#x9;Restricted&#xD;txtSubTitle=A Framework for Quantitative Reliability Assessment ofÃ¿&#xA;Subsurface Containment&#xD;txtKeyWords=CCS, CO2, Sour Gas, Containment, Probability, Reliability, Risk Assessment, Geomechanics&#xD;txtDocNo2=11&#xD;txtDocNo3=13087&#xD;cboECCNNumber=7&#x9;Non US - Non Controlled&#xD;cboDateOfIssueMonth=0&#x9;January&#xD;cboDateOfIssueYear=10&#x9;2012&#xD;cboLocation=4&#x9;P&amp;T Rijswijk (GS)&#xD;txtAddress=&#xD;txtWBSEcode=ZZPT/010397/01.01&#xD;txtPeriodOfWork=January - December 2011&#xD;chkDocumentHistory=False&#xD;autName=P.A.J. van den Bogert&#xD;autRefInd=PTI/RC&#xD;revName=P.A. Fokker&#xD;revRefInd=PTI/RC &#xD;revName=W. Pao &#xD;revRefInd=PTI/RC &#xD;revName=C.J. Otto&#xD;revRefInd=PTI/RC &#xD;aprName=C.J. Otto&#xD;aprRefInd=PTI/RC&#xD;nonName=nothing&#xD;nonRefInd=nothing&#xD;</pdfx:Comments>
         <pdfx:ShellDivision>SIEP Rijswijk</pdfx:ShellDivision>
         <pdfx:frmDivision/>
         <pdfx:frmCover>Cover Screen&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;All data entered on this screen will go onto the cover page of the report. When you press the OK button, automatic formatting will be applied, so that the cover page complies to Shell standard formatting.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Please do not make manual chang</pdfx:frmCover>
         <pdfx:frmCover1>For a full help file please consult our web site (click on link below)</pdfx:frmCover1>
         <pdfx:frmCover2/>
         <pdfx:frmCover3/>
         <pdfx:frmCover4/>
         <pdfx:frmCrossRef>Insert Help text here, please</pdfx:frmCrossRef>
         <pdfx:frmCrossRef1>For information about this subject, please consult Sue Baak or Johan Josee by email:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;siep-reportsrijswijk&#xD;&#xA;</pdfx:frmCrossRef1>
         <pdfx:frmCaptionProperties>Insert Help text here, please</pdfx:frmCaptionProperties>
         <pdfx:frmCaptionProperties1>For information about this subject, please consult Sue Baak or Johan Josee by email:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;siep-reportsrijswijk&#xD;&#xA;</pdfx:frmCaptionProperties1>
         <pdfx:frmDivision1>Division Selection Screen&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Several items in a standard report differ division by division. By selecting the appropriate division you tell the template to take the required style of your own division into account.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Creating a template for another divis</pdfx:frmDivision1>
         <pdfx:frmDivision2>ion is easy:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;1. Double-click on the Cover Screen&#xD;&#xA;2. Select the appropriate division&#xD;&#xA;3. Click OK&#xD;&#xA;4. Use Explorer to make a copy of the .dot file&#xD;&#xA;5. Rename it properly (e.g. SIEP Houston.dot)</pdfx:frmDivision2>
         <pdfx:frmLitRef1>For information about this subject, please consult Sue Baak or Johan Josee by email:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;siep-reportsrijswijk&#xD;&#xA;</pdfx:frmLitRef1>
         <pdfx:frmPrint1>In order to have the right kind of tables in your report, you should use this menu to indicate which tables you want to have.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Important notice:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;NEVER manually try to remove one or more of the tables mentioned, nor make manual changes to their appear</pdfx:frmPrint1>
         <pdfx:TemplateVersion>8.0</pdfx:TemplateVersion>
         <pdfx:OrgUpdateFieldsAtPrint>1</pdfx:OrgUpdateFieldsAtPrint>
         <pdfx:frmCaptionProperties2/>
         <pdfx:frmCaptionProperties3/>
         <pdfx:frmCrossRef2/>
         <pdfx:frmCrossRef3/>
         <pdfx:frmCrossRef4/>
         <pdfx:frmLitRef2/>
         <pdfx:frmLitRef3/>
         <pdfx:frmLitRef4/>
         <pdfx:frmLitRef5/>
         <pdfx:frmLitRef6/>
         <pdfx:frmLitRef7/>
         <pdfx:frmLitRef8/>
         <pdfx:frmPrint2>ance or contents. This could mean that automatic insertion of a table will fail or at least that the document will not conform to Shell house style.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;This 'Preview'/'Print' menu presents three options:&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;1 - Update Table Of Contents:&#xD;&#xA;In some situati</pdfx:frmPrint2>
         <pdfx:frmPrint3>ons you don't want Word to make a new table of contents before printing. You cannot choose to remove the table as a whole, because Shell house style dictates the use of a table of contents.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;2 - Insert List Of Tables:&#xD;&#xA;Only if one or more numbered table</pdfx:frmPrint3>
         <pdfx:frmPrint4>s are present in the report, this option will be shown. If you have before chosen to insert a List Of Tables, you can remove it by turning this option off and vice versa. The contents of the List Of Tables will always be updated before the report is sent </pdfx:frmPrint4>
         <pdfx:frmPrint5>to the printer.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;3 - Insert List Of Figures:&#xD;&#xA;Analogous to the second option. This option too, will only appear if any numbered figures are found in the report.&#xD;&#xA;</pdfx:frmPrint5>
         <pdfx:Location>P&amp;T Rijswijk (GS)</pdfx:Location>
         <pdfx:frmCaptionProperties4/>
         <pdfx:frmCaptionProperties5/>
